<%# A single headline figure with its label.

    Stripe reading: the number is the content, so it gets the size and weight and
    the label stays quiet above it. Figures use tabular-nums so a row of stats
    lines up rather than jittering.

    Built with tag.div rather than a literal element because the optional
    data-testid has to be omitted entirely when absent - interpolating it into the
    markup produced an unquoted attribute that selectors could not match.

    Locals:
      label  - what the figure is
      value  - the figure, already formatted
      hint   - optional supporting line
      testid - optional data-testid, for tests targeting a specific stat %>
<%# .tw-card, not its own rounded-xl / shadow-xs surface. This was a fourth card treatment: the
    portfolio page put three of these beside a .tw-card chart, a .tw-card summary and a
    hand-rolled h-[150px] panel, so four radii and three shadows shared one screen. %>
<%= tag.div class: "tw-card p-5",
            data: { testid: local_assigns[:testid] } do %>
  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600"><%= label %></p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums"><%= value %></p>
  <% if local_assigns[:hint].present? %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500"><%= hint %></p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
